course: dictionary
lesson: 11968
title: Sorting things into categories
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A category is a group of things that are alike in some way. When you sort things into categories, you put the ones that go together in the same group. «Put the animals into categories» means sort them into groups such as birds, fish and insects.
explain: Look for the clue that links the things. Cats, dogs and rabbits are all mammals, so they fall into the same category. A snake and a lizard are reptiles, so they fall into a different category. Ask yourself: what do these things have in common?
explain: In a competition, a category is a class, a separate group that people enter. «The under-10 category» means only children aged under 10 compete in that group. Each category has its own winners.
fact: A category is a group of things or people that are alike in some way.
fact: Phrases to know: fall into a category, or be in the category of something.
fact: In maths and science you might sort numbers into odd and even, or matter into solids, liquids and gases.
fact: A bar chart shows how many items are in each category.
fact: «The under-10 category» means a class in a competition for children under 10.
exercise: «Put the animals into categories.» What is a category here? | A noisy farm | A cage for the animals | *A group of things that are alike in some way | A single animal on its own
exercise: Cats, dogs and rabbits are all mammals. Which category do they fall into? | Reptiles | *Mammals | Gases | Odd numbers
exercise: «The under-10 category» is a race for whom? | Adults over 50 | *Children aged under 10 | Dogs and cats | Only the fastest runner in the school
test: In a bar chart, what does each bar show? | The name of the teacher | The colour of each group | The date | *How many items are in each category
test: Which number would go in the odd category? | 4 | 6 | 8 | *7
exam: «Sort the animals into categories: birds, fish and insects.» What is a category? | A kind of race | A test with marks out of ten | *A group of things that are alike in some way | A word that means very big
